{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774027004,"nonce":"/Mw5NAJTyU7j+4mZ5nH7kUqUcDA=","message":"**Round 3 synthesis — continuations, issue hub, surface binding, SDK tiers**\n\nTwo independent analyses (Opus + Gemini) converged on all points:\n\n**Continuations**: Dissolved into work-unit model. Handoff notes live on the work unit, not the session. Auto-acked when a new session picks up the issue. Primary action is \"Resume\" (spawn SDK agent with context), not \"Acknowledge\". Inbox becomes notification pointers to issues, not a parallel data store.\n\n**Issue as navigation hub**: Unified detail view with status banner, activity timeline (sessions + auth + comments + handoff notes merged chronologically), related entity chips, branch info, and contextual actions (Resume/Start Agent/Open in Console/View History/View Auth). New endpoint: GET /api/issues/:repo/:id/context.\n\n**Surface binding**: Shared EntityPill component for universal cross-linking. One-click-to-hub from any tab. Missing links identified: Conversations and Projects tabs are complete islands. No global sidebar (each tab owns its detail view).\n\n**SDK-first tiers**:\n- T1 (SDK): full lifecycle + structured introspection. Default for Resume.\n- T2 (PTY): process control + terminal I/O.\n- T3 (External): best-effort discovery.\n\"Resume\" always upgrades to T1. SDK-only: permissions, cost tracking, branching, auto-resume. Universal: issue linking, liveness, auth, branches.\n\n**No disagreements between agents.** Ready for implementation planning.","files":null}]}